# apps/web rules

## Stack

- Next.js 15 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui.
- `@tableau/embedding-api-react` pinned to the Tableau Cloud minor version.
- NextAuth (Auth.js v5) for portal auth.
- `jose` for JWT signing.

## Routing & tenancy

- All tenant-scoped pages: `apps/web/app/t/[tenantSlug]/...`.
- Middleware (`apps/web/middleware.ts`) MUST verify `tenantSlug === session.user.tenantId` (or the user has the `internal-employees` group) for every `/t/...` request.
- `/api/tableau/token` and `/api/chat` are tenant-aware: derive tenant from session, not from URL/body.

## Tableau embedding

- Use `<TableauViz>` and `<TableauPulse>` from `@tableau/embedding-api-react`.
- Mint the JWT in a server action or route handler (`/api/tableau/token`), pass to client components.
- **Reuse one JWT** across all Tableau components on a page.
- Add `onVizLoadError` to detect auth issues and trigger a token refetch.
- See `.claude/skills/tableau-embed-component/` and `.claude/docs/embedding-api-cheatsheet.md`.

## Agent chat

- `/api/chat` uses the Anthropic SDK with native MCP `mcp_servers` parameter.
- Pre-fetch `get-datasource-metadata` and inject the field list into the system prompt before the first LLM call.
- Constrain the toolset via `packages/mcp-tools/allowlist.ts`.
- Stream SSE; never buffer full responses.
- Forward the end-user identity to the MCP server as `Tableau-User`.

## Validation

- Every Route Handler validates its request body with Zod at the top.
- Never trust `searchParams` or `params` without parsing.

## Don't

- Don't import server-only modules into client components.
- Don't cache JWTs across users.
- Don't use `any`. Don't use `as` to launder untyped data — narrow it.
- Don't add a new `/api/...` route without security-reviewer subagent review.
